# Panel Review Adapter

Use this rule when the user asks to convene a panel, run a panel review, get
expert eyes, pressure-test a doc/plan/spec/decision, or get red-team feedback.

If the panel skill checkout is available, read `references/cursor.md` there for
the complete Cursor workflow. Use `panel-preflight.js` from the same checkout
when available so mode detection, decline routing, PII screening, and cost gates
match the Claude Code and Codex adapters.

Cursor orchestration summary:

1. Resolve mode: artifact or document-like text means Review; scoped open
   question means Council; `review:` and `council:` override; `thorough` opts
   into the deeper run.
2. Apply decline, PII, and cost gates before running any lens.
3. Select 3-5 genuinely distinct lenses from `skeptic`, `enduser`, `rigor`,
   `feasibility`, `simplicity`, `risk`, `completeness`, and `strategic`; add at
   most 1-2 ad-hoc niche lenses when needed.
4. Run each lens independently and keep outputs separated. Cursor should use a
   serial pass unless the active environment provides an explicit parallel-agent
   mechanism.
5. Batch pressure-test findings. Do not verify one agent per finding.
6. Synthesize a ranked, edit-ready Review report or a Council recommendation
   with tradeoffs and dissent.

The panel is a critic and decider, not a blank-page generator.
